        best_serialized = None

        for preference in preferences:
            order = self._repair(
                width,
                preference,
                columns,
                one_way_dep,
                blocks,
            )
            serialized = self._serialize(text, order)
            score = self._score(serialized)
            if score > best_score:
                best_score = score
                best_order = order
                best_serialized = serialized

        result, public_orders = self._materialize(
            df,
            source,
            best_order,
            best_serialized,
        )

        if result.shape != df.shape:
            raise RuntimeError("Reordering changed DataFrame shape")

        self._last_orders = public_orders
        return result, public_orders
```

The main change is replacing the previous path/beam construction with disjoint affinity packets. Affinity is evaluated only among the 20 highest repetition-mass blocks, and at most ten pairs are accepted greedily. Two complete packet layouts are then scored: the selected orientation and its reversed packet orientation. The global frequency-ranked layout remains as the incumbent fallback, while all candidates are evaluated using the exact sorted-row character LCP objective.
